b=Book('05','Railway Deployment & Operations','Deployment-Security-Operations','Reproducible deployment, configuration, scheduled work, security boundaries, monitoring and recovery.');b.intro()
b.section('Confirmed hosting and deployment boundary','''Railway is owner-confirmed as the current host. The repository's root Dockerfile builds the main Next.js app; it does not by itself provision Supabase, R2, third-party OAuth apps, payment webhooks, schedules or optional Python/SDR services. Exact Railway project IDs, services, regions, replicas, resource sizes and deployed commit were not available to this audit.

Use this volume as a source-based operating recipe, not a claim that all steps are already applied to production. Existing Amplify configuration and older deployment ADRs remain repository artifacts, but are not adopted here as the production runbook. Do not redeploy to those platforms just because an old guide names them.

A deployable release is a compatible application build, database migration state, environment configuration, provider permissions, callback configuration, worker/scheduler availability and a recoverable previous release. Record all of those together. A green container build is not sufficient evidence that generation, payment, media access or scheduled delivery works.''',('Dockerfile','next.config.ts','src/server/env.ts','docs/deployment-guide.md'))
b.section('Container build and runtime requirements','''The Dockerfile uses Node 22 on Debian bookworm-slim in dependency, builder and runner stages. It installs dependencies from package-lock, builds Next.js, verifies the Clarity build, then copies standalone output, public assets, static chunks and vendor resources into the runtime image. The runtime uses a non-root nextjs user.

The final image includes Chromium and fonts for visual capture/render fallback, Python and ExifTool for image metadata, and FFmpeg for video assembly. GEO_RENDER_EXECUTABLE and VISUAL_CAPTURE_BROWSER_PATH point to the installed Chromium. If using a different Railway build strategy, reproduce those native runtime dependencies; package.json alone does not install them.

The process binds to HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0 and Railway's injected PORT. The Docker health command checks /health on that port. /api/health exposes safe capability and build identity; /api/health/ready is a deeper readiness surface. /health is the simple process endpoint and must not be mistaken for provider or database readiness.

Public NEXT_PUBLIC values are build inputs and can be embedded in client bundles. Provider and service-role secrets are runtime server values. Never place secret keys in build-public variables merely to make a browser feature connect. Changing a build-public URL generally requires rebuilding the client artifact.''',('Dockerfile','src/app/health/route.ts','src/app/api/health/route.ts','src/app/api/health/ready/route.ts','scripts/start-production.mjs'))
b.section('Recommended fresh-environment deployment sequence')
b.table(['Step','Action','Exit evidence'],[['1. Freeze release','Record commit, lockfile, migration list and provider policy.','Release manifest with approved environment target.'],['2. Provision state','Create isolated Supabase project, private R2 bucket and optional Redis.','Correct project IDs and access boundaries, without exposing secrets.'],['3. Apply schema','Verify and apply the canonical migration sequence to the new target.','Recorded migration history and regenerated/checked types.'],['4. Configure secrets','Set required core runtime values, encryption roots, provider keys and callback origins.','Production env validation and deliberate optional-feature readiness.'],['5. Build on Railway','Use root Dockerfile or equivalent dependency-complete build.','Build succeeds; standalone assets and native tools present.'],['6. Verify process','Bind PORT; configure Railway health path and custom HTTPS origin.','/health responds, deployed identity matches expected commit.'],['7. Wire providers','Set exact OAuth redirects, signed webhook endpoints and intended scopes.','Test account connection and webhook validation.'],['8. Enable schedules','Verify database/network cron target and secret; check heartbeat.','Due job advances exactly once without opening public writes.'],['9. Smoke test','Use a controlled workspace and permitted provider operations.','Auth isolation, content, media, balance and delivery evidence.'],['10. Release gates','Enable features deliberately, observe errors/cost and retain rollback.','Stable key paths plus recoverable previous release.']],[.8,2.6,2])
