b.section('Required configuration and encryption continuity','''Core server validation requires APP_URL, Supabase URL/publishable/service-role values, matching browser-safe Supabase values, OPENROUTER_API_KEY and CRON_SECRET. In production APP_URL must be the intended HTTPS origin rather than localhost. The catalog, callbacks, consent metadata and generated links depend on it. Refer to src/server/env.ts for current validation; some feature-specific modules validate additional variables outside that central schema.

R2 needs account ID, access key ID, secret access key and bucket name. An endpoint override is optional. A partially configured set fails explicitly rather than silently moving production media into another backend. The production storage path requires R2, while development can use legacy Supabase fallback.

Google, GitHub, WordPress, Webflow, Canva, Notion and Slack each have their own OAuth/app configuration. Google sign-in credentials are distinct from Google Analytics/Search Console authorization. Register exact callback origins and paths. Preserve connector encryption roots across releases; a rotated key without a migration can strand saved grants.

For distribution select Post for Me when intended and configure its key/webhook secret. SocialAPI is retired. SDR is optional and needs its own endpoint, tenant provisioning, secrets and workspace flag if selected. For billing, production defaults to enforcement on; payment keys, webhook secret, price mappings and schema readiness still need verification.''',('src/server/env.ts','src/server/assets/storage.server.ts','src/server/connectors','src/server/billing/readiness.server.ts','src/lib/feature-flags.ts'))
b.section('Feature switches and readiness')
b.table(['Feature','Source default / prerequisite','Operational consequence'],[['Autopilot','On unless false; plan and program setup still apply','Full automatic mode has its own flag; AGENTS_DISABLED/workspace pause can stop execution.'],['Audience','On unless false; separate auto-score flag','Worker reads existing shared scheduler; disabled mode hides/blocks feature paths.'],['Memory / chat tools','On unless false; workspace memory switch separately','Do not bypass editor/admin write rules.'],['MCP','Global gate on unless false; per-workspace access starts off','Admin enables access and separately permits changes.'],['Stories','On unless false, with workspace override','Requires Story schema plus account permissions; preserve frame recovery.'],['GEO scan probes','Explicit opt-in','Paid multi-engine checks; not the same switch as tracked-prompt allowances.'],['GEO rendering','Explicit configured fallback','Chromium and safe resource fetching required.'],['Proof Engine','Explicit opt-in','Plan and eligibility checks still apply.'],['Slack','Explicit opt-in','Provider installation and verified inbound binding required.'],['UGC','KIE prerequisite in current legacy helper plus feature gate','Runtime health/provider readiness is not identical to this helper; verify OpenRouter-only deployments carefully.'],['Canva Magic Layers','Preview flag should be false for public integration review','Flat-image fallback is a separate supported path.'],['Platform DB flags','Env override, then database rule, otherwise off','Fifteen-second cache; does not replace all older env gates.']],[1,1.8,2.3])
b.p('Do not assume one universal flag system. Current code includes legacy environment gates, workspace overrides, account entitlements and newer database rollout flags. Platform flags, model-route overrides, spend caps and operational switches have separate services and caches. Confirm the gate used by the exact feature path.')
