b.h('Shared minute scheduler')
b.p('run-schedules expects a sixty-second cadence. It runs up to twenty-five due scheduled jobs and twenty-five due Market Brain collections, Autopilot with a forty-five-second/max-twelve sweep, and Audience with a forty-second/max-six sweep. after() continuations refresh trends if due, collect audience outcomes, run bounded visual captures and purge expired memories. These continuations still require process time; deployments/restarts make durable recovery important.');b.source('src/app/api/public/hooks/run-schedules/route.ts')
b.section('Security boundaries and control matrix')
b.table(['Boundary','Implemented control','Verification to preserve'],[['User identity','Supabase verified bearer/cookie session flows','Invalid recovery link cannot use an unrelated session.'],['Tenant access','Explicit workspace membership/role plus RLS','Outsider IDs and stale workspace context are rejected.'],['Service role','Server-only explicit privileged clients','Every privileged query is scoped and audited.'],['External fetch','DNS/private-address protection, redirect validation, size/time bounds','Block metadata/private hosts and redirect pivots.'],['Media','Workspace paths, signatures, prompt/image/video safety','Uploads and edits cannot bypass publish-time review.'],['OAuth','Bound one-use state, expiry, PKCE/cookie where implemented','Wrong browser/user/workspace and replay fail.'],['Webhooks','Raw-body signature/secret checks and replay-safe transitions','Invalid/stale messages cannot advance state.'],['Payment','Server pricing, holds, signed events, idempotent grants','Browser amount and success-page visit are not authority.'],['Repository writes','Verified source host, reviewed base and patch approval','No direct push/merge to protected base by a generator.'],['External assistants','Workspace gate, caller role, own app checks and audit','Unapproved content cannot be published via MCP.'],['Staff tools','Permissions, production MFA, recent MFA for sensitive actions','A customer admin is not automatically platform staff.']],[1,2.4,2]);b.source('src/server/route.ts','src/server/safe-fetch.ts','src/server/guardrails','src/server/mcp','src/server/admin/route.ts')
b.section('Headers, browser sessions and privacy','''next.config.ts sets CSP and security headers, API no-store behavior, frame restrictions, MIME-sniff prevention, referrer policy and production HSTS. The CSP retains unsafe-inline for required framework bootstrapping and JSON-LD; do not describe it as a strict per-request nonce policy. Allowed connect/frame hosts are deliberate integration requirements.

The Supabase browser client manages the current session flow, including legacy-session migration and explicit callback handling. Do not generalize an older localStorage description over the current cookie/SSR behavior. Client storage and UI guards do not replace server session verification.

Sensitive credential data belongs in server-only tables with encryption and minimal safe metadata exposed to clients. Helicone prompt-body logging is opt-in; telemetry configuration can affect data exposure. The repository does not establish a universal retention period, data residency guarantee, certified compliance status, signed data-processing contract or backup erasure guarantee. Those remain documented owner decisions, not assumptions.''',('next.config.ts','src/integrations/supabase/client.ts','docs/security.md','docs/privacy.md','docs/self-hosted-integrations.md'))
b.section('Monitoring, readiness and incident triage','''Start with /health for process liveness, /api/health for safe build/capability information and /api/health/ready for configured readiness. The health version uses Railway/Git commit metadata and process start time. A configured key is not proof that the vendor account is funded or an API request succeeds.

Useful durable signals include AI usage/reservations, billing holds and financial events, cron heartbeats, job status/lease age, webhook events, audit logs, provider failures, missing connections and queue lag. Optional Sentry, Helicone, Redis and alert sinks improve observability when configured. Track pending-job age and capture/release failures as well as HTTP error rate.

During an incident identify the affected release and workspace safely, check recent configuration/migration changes, isolate provider outage versus auth/credit/rate/safety failure, and disable the smallest affected feature path if necessary. Reconcile uncertain side effects from stored provider IDs and event history before retrying. Never repair a dashboard by manually marking an unknown post delivered or a GEO finding verified.''',('src/app/api/health/route.ts','src/app/api/health/ready/route.ts','src/server/observability','src/server/cron.ts','docs/operations.md'))
b.table(['Symptom','First checks','Safe recovery'],[['App fails at boot','Required env validation, public build args, schema readiness','Restore correct config/release; keep encryption roots stable.'],['Jobs never advance','Heartbeat, scheduler target/secret, lease expiry, flags','Repair scheduler then bounded idempotent sweep.'],['Video stuck after deploy','Stored provider task, composition row, FFmpeg, poll route','Resume accepted tasks; do not submit blindly.'],['Media 403/404','Workspace path, storage backend marker, expired URL, R2 config','Re-sign through authorized route; preserve old objects.'],['Unexpected charge/balance','Hold/capture/event key, webhook history, allowance window','Reconcile ledger; use audited adjustment rather than duplicate grant.'],['Published twice','Provider IDs, retries, uncertain timeout and callback ordering','Stop repeated submit; reconcile each accepted publication.'],['OAuth needs attention','Callback exact origin, encrypted grant, scope and revocation','Reconnect only after configuration/key issue understood.'],['Scan fails or is empty','SSRF block, robots, crawl stage, rendering gate and limits','Explain the blocked target; do not weaken safe-fetch globally.']],[1.2,2,2])
b.section('Backups, rollback and storage migration','''Recommended backup scope is PostgreSQL schema/data and migration history, private media and its mapping identities, environment/encryption-key escrow, provider installation metadata and release artifacts. The actual backup provider, region, schedule, retention, restore test, RPO and RTO were not supplied. Set those explicitly before claiming disaster recovery readiness.

Application rollback on Railway should restore the last known healthy deployment or a reviewed revert. Database changes may not be backward compatible; prefer additive migrations and verify the old application can read the new schema before relying on deploy rollback. Never run an improvised reverse migration against a production ledger.

Keep R2 credentials available during rollback so assets created after cutover remain readable. Legacy Supabase objects and migration aliases may still be referenced. Storage migration uses checkpoints, checksums, reference cutover and rollback controls; do not delete old objects merely because copying finished. Retirement requires separate verification and authorization.

A recovery drill should restore into an isolated environment, validate memberships/RLS, reopen representative old and new assets, advance a paused durable job, check financial replay behavior and verify callback URLs cannot reach production accidentally. Record evidence and elapsed time rather than a guessed availability promise.''',('docs/storage-migration.md','docs/storage.md','supabase/migrations','docs/operations.md'))
b.section('Environment name inventory',new=True)
b.p('Names only. No secret values were read from private .env files. The list combines literal process.env references in non-test TypeScript with keys in .env.example. Template-only entries may be old, optional or read indirectly; they are not proof of active use or required production settings. Dynamic families such as AI_MODEL_<ROUTE>, AI_PRICE_<MODEL> and workspace flag overrides require the family rules in the relevant module.')
def category(k):
    if k.startswith('NEXT_PUBLIC_'):return 'Public build/browser value'
    if k.startswith('FEATURE_FLAG_'):return 'Feature gate; inspect owning helper'
    if any(x in k for x in ['SECRET','PRIVATE_KEY','API_KEY','TOKEN','PASSWORD']):return 'Sensitive server configuration'
    if k.startswith(('AI_','UGC_','VIDEO_','IMAGE_','GEO_')):return 'AI/media/routing control'
    if k.startswith(('BILLING_','STRIPE_','MELLOX_LINK','MELLOX_CREDITS')):return 'Financial/entitlement configuration'
    return 'Server/integration/runtime configuration'
keys=sorted(set(D['envrefs'])|set(D['templateKeys']))
b.table(['Variable name','Classification','Evidence'],[[k,category(k),'Source: '+D['envrefs'][k][0] if k in D['envrefs'] else '.env.example name only'] for k in keys],[1.7,1.25,2]);b.source('.env.example','src/server/env.ts')
